  "verse": 28,
  "plain_english": "`pilot_V2N_ARGUMENT_MAP.md`. Dyczkowski-mode.*\n\n**The inner appearance stands firm — for every living one**\n\nThe ṣaṣṭho vimarśa, on the power of removal, comes to its close; and its final claim is one of\nunfailing constancy. The inner appearance — the self-grasp, the reflexive-awareness — stands firm in\nmemory, in construction, and in cognition alike (kārikā 8). It is not something that flickers in and\nout, present in cognition and absent in memory. It is the one light that runs through them all. In the\ncognition whose form is the external manifestation, this inner appearance — the prior-experience-form —\nis innate (kārikā 9); and it stands, too, in memory and the rest. In the freely-wandering construction,\nthe inner appearance is innate indeed (kārikā 10): the construction may wander at will, forming this or\nthat shape, but the self-grasp that shapes it is always there, in the mind's range. And hence — from the\nmanifestation of the uplifting as wished — knowledge and action are clear, established for every living\none (kārikā 11).\n\nAnd this constancy extends even to the freed. Even in liberation, the freed souls (muktāṇava) are\ndistinct — yet their manifestation, by the śiva-ness, is the un-broken all-knowing. The three-time\nmanifestation may be established in the māyīya knower, but it does not fail to flash for them either,\nfrom their all-knowing. And the mantreśvaras — even in liberation, by the exhaustion of their authority,\nin the place of the other — by the word-obtaining (the dīkṣā, the vow, the japa, the tapas, the\nconcentration, the conduct), transmigrating, are all-knowing; the knower-ness is not de-valued. The\nanimal-atoms are distinct only in their animal-ness, generally. The categories, the worlds, the\nelements, the kalā, the mantra, the word, the phoneme — the jars and the rest, with respect to their\nown class, are not utterly unprecedented.\n\nThe objection \"how, in the dealing-time, is the creation?\" is met. The creation is by the unity — at\nthat time, per-knower, the jar-appearance and the body-appearance are distinct, but the consciousness-\nself alone [creates them]; and the knower-distinction is not destroyed, for it stands in the\nprāṇa-puryaṣṭaka and the like. And the appearance is the cognition: the jar-form appearance, though\nknown, is of the knower-operation-form, of the knower-standing-ness — it is the cognition itself. The\nfinal objection — \"then by the knower's will, per-moment the creation and withdrawal of objects and\nknowers — how does the maheśvara shine?\" — is answered: the order-word's pure-form-sequence is not the\nwhole; the maheśvara, the Lord, is the one who shines through it all.\n\nSo the vimarśa closes with the constancy of the self-grasp. It is innate in memory, in cognition, in\nconstruction; it stands firm for the bound and for the freed, for the animal-atom and the mantreśvara;\nand from its manifestation — the uplifting as wished — knowledge and action are clear for every living\none. The inner appearance, the reflexive-awareness, never fails: it is the very nature of the light,\nand it is what makes every living one a knower and a doer. The apohanaśaktivimarśa — the reflexion on\nthe power of removal — here comes to its close.\n\n- **Preserved:** kārikā 8 (the inner appearance stands firm in memory/construction/cognition);\n  kārikā 9 (the innate inner appearance in the external-form cognition, standing in memory etc.);\n  kārikā 10 (the innate in the freely-wandering construction); kārikā 11 (the uplifting-as-wished,\n  knowledge and action clear for every living one); the muktāṇava distinct yet all-knowing; the\n  three-time manifestation; the mantreśvara (the word-obtaining, the dīkṣā etc., the transmigration,\n  the all-knowing); the paśvaṇūṇa; the tattvabhuvanādayaḥ; the jars not utterly unprecedented; the\n  \"not then-created and then-withdrawn\"; the prior-created-ness; the creation by the unity; the\n  knower-distinction not destroyed (the prāṇa-puryaṣṭaka); the appearance as the cognition (the\n  knower-operation-form); the per-moment creation objection and the maheśvara-shines answer; the\n  ||6|| colophon.\n- **Added (SUPPLIED, recoverable):** \"the self-grasp that shapes it is always there\" (the free\n  construction); \"the inner appearance … never fails\" (the constancy); \"it is what makes every living\n  one a knower and a doer\" (kārikā 11). Interpretive unpacking, not new doctrine.\n- **NOT resolved:** the vāsanāprabodha-sūtra citations' exact frames; the traiyambaka. Logged, not\n  invented.\nEOF\necho \"V2N L2: $(wc -l < /mnt/HC_Volume_106427611/sanskritree/translations/_stack/ipvv/pilot/pilot_V2N_L2_read.md) lines\"",
